WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.570
In this video we are going to talk about
collision detection and collision

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:08.910
avoidance. So before we do that, let's
imagine there's a room and there are,

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:13.320
like, three different people and when two
people are talking, the third person, if

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:17.160
he tries to talk, the conversation
becomes difficult for the other two

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.260
people. In the same way,

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:24.600
let's say we have three different
computers on the same network. Now if A

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:32.700
was talking to B and C suddenly
transfers data to A there is a

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:37.380
collision and when this collision
happens the original message from A to B

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:39.180
becomes garbage.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:42.930
It's of no use anymore because there is
interference. So when there is a

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:48.690
collision that happens A detects it and
it backs off before it tries to send a

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:53.879
message back to B again. So this was in
the original days of the networking but

00:00:53.879 --> 00:00:54.899
later

00:00:54.899 --> 00:01:00.840
what happened is, they added the concept of collision avoidance. So in that, what

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:07.530
happens is: C, before it actually
starts sending data to A, it tries to see

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:13.530
if there is a conversation going on
already before it sends. So that's CA

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:14.700
or Collision Avoidance.

